## ResticHub @VERSION@

### Contents

- The control plane image `@IMAGE@` for linux/amd64 and linux/arm64.
- `install.sh` and the deploy archive `restichub-deploy-@VERSION@.tar.gz`: the files of the control plane server.
- The agent packages for Linux (amd64, arm64; static musl builds) and Windows (amd64).
- One CycloneDX SBOM for each package and each image.
- `SHA256SUMS` for every file of this release.
- A `.sigstore.json` bundle for every file: the keyless cosign signature.

### Install the control plane

Run the script of this release as root on a new server:

```sh
curl -fsSL https://github.com/@REPO@/releases/download/@TAG@/install.sh | sudo bash -s -- --domain restichub.example.com --email admin@example.com
```

Upgrade an installed server with `install.sh --upgrade`. The script verifies the deploy archive and the image with the identity below. The SHA-256 of the files:

- `install.sh`: `@INSTALL_SHA256@`
- `restichub-deploy-@VERSION@.tar.gz`: `@DEPLOY_SHA256@`

### Verify

Every signature comes from the GitHub OIDC identity of the release workflow for the tag `@TAG@`. See the verification guide: https://github.com/@REPO@/blob/@TAG@/docs/src/content/docs/operations/verify-a-release.md

```sh
cosign verify-blob \
  --bundle SHA256SUMS.sigstore.json \
  --certificate-identity "https://github.com/@REPO@/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/tags/@TAG@" \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com \
  SHA256SUMS
sha256sum --check --ignore-missing SHA256SUMS

cosign verify \
  --certificate-identity "https://github.com/@REPO@/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/tags/@TAG@" \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com \
  @IMAGE@
```

